      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "ig-artifact-ingestion"
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "ig-artifact-ingestion",
      "dcterms:source": "smart-base/skills/content/authoring-who-smart-guidelines/ig-artifact-ingestion.md",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-base/v0/ns/glossary/kg-skills/indicator-extraction",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-base/v0/ns/glossary/kg-skills"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "indicator-extraction"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Extract the indicators an L1 source prints (indicator reference or metadata sheets: name, numerator, denominator, disaggregation, definition, data sources) as L1 `indicator` nodes with every printed field, then draft one L2 program indicator per indicator, derived from its L1 node. Read before adding a WHO handbook's or guideline's indicators to a DAK or a DTH, and whenever an L2 indicator has to trace to its source. Part of L1 → L2 extraction for every DAK and DTH, beside recommendation-extraction."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "indicator-extraction",
      "dcterms:source": "smart-base/skills/content/authoring-who-smart-guidelines/indicator-extraction.md",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-base/v0/ns/glossary/kg-skills/inform-client",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-base/v0/ns/glossary/kg-skills"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "inform-client"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "A health worker tells the client (or caregiver) what was decided and what happens next, in words and, where the DAK gives one, on a slip or card: a referral, a return date, a result. Input is what to tell and the client's language; output is that the client was told, and what they were handed. Generic for any DAK step that ends with the client being informed."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "inform-client",
      "dcterms:source": "smart-base/skills/content/authoring-who-smart-guidelines/inform-client.md",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-base/v0/ns/glossary/kg-skills/l2-component-edit-review",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-base/v0/ns/glossary/kg-skills"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "l2-component-edit-review"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "How one L2 DAK component is edited by the agent and reviewed by a person: personas and user scenarios, BPMN business processes, DMN decision and scheduling logic, core data elements and glossary with their terminology bindings, indicators and requirements. One subprocess for all of them. The agent edits, checks, renders and stages with a before/after, then hands the component on, and review forks alongside it without blocking. Per component, it lists the authoring skill, checker, renderer and diff, reviewing role, and what the reviewer judges. Read before authoring or reviewing any L2 component, and when an L2 track asks what its reviewer needs to see."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "l2-component-edit-review",
      "dcterms:source": "smart-base/skills/content/authoring-who-smart-guidelines/l2-component-edit-review.md",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-base/v0/ns/glossary/kg-skills/l2-dak-authoring",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-base/v0/ns/glossary/kg-skills"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "l2-dak-authoring"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Author the L2 layer of a WHO SMART Guideline — the Digital Adaptation Kit between the narrative L1 guideline and the L3 FHIR artefacts — one DAK component per pass (personas, user scenarios, business processes, data dictionary, decision and scheduling logic, indicators, requirements), each edited and then reviewed alongside through l2-component-edit-review. Stage 4 of smart-guideline-end-to-end and the authoring steps of l2-dak-authoring.bpmn. Read before authoring or adapting any DAK component."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "l2-dak-authoring",
      "dcterms:source": "smart-base/skills/content/authoring-who-smart-guidelines/l2-dak-authoring.md",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-base/v0/ns/glossary/kg-skills/l2-dependency-choice",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-base/v0/ns/glossary/kg-skills"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "l2-dependency-choice"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Stage 3 of smart-guideline-end-to-end: choose which existing DAKs (WHO's, or a jurisdiction's adaptation) the guideline builds on. From the L1 knowledge graph and any known candidates, one decision row per candidate DAK — reuse, adapt, extend or reject, with evidence and a reason — laid out as a decision-comparison table and put to the adjudicators as a DecisionRequest. Also defines the dependency decision row that stage 5 (l3-dependency-choice) uses at L3. Read before choosing, or recording, a DAK dependency."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "l2-dependency-choice",
      "dcterms:source": "smart-base/skills/content/authoring-who-smart-guidelines/l2-dependency-choice.md",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-base/v0/ns/glossary/kg-skills/l3-dependency-choice",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-base/v0/ns/glossary/kg-skills"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "l3-dependency-choice"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Stage 5 of smart-guideline-end-to-end: choose which existing FHIR IGs (WHO's, or a jurisdiction's) the guideline's L3 builds on. Indexes each candidate IG with ig-artifact-ingestion, matches the L1 knowledge graph and the stage-4 L2 assets against the index, and returns one decision row per IG naming the profiles, value sets and libraries reused, derived from or not used. Read before choosing, or recording, an IG dependency."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "l3-dependency-choice",
      "dcterms:source": "smart-base/skills/content/authoring-who-smart-guidelines/l3-dependency-choice.md",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-base/v0/ns/glossary/kg-skills/l3-readiness",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-base/v0/ns/glossary/kg-skills"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "l3-readiness"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "The check between stages 5 and 6 of smart-guideline-end-to-end (Gateway_L3Ready): may the agent write L3 assets yet? Yes only when every source of the use case has its L1 extraction, every L2 asset names the L1 node it rests on, every L3 artefact about to be written names the L2 asset it implements, and the review of each extraction and L2 asset has been requested. Returns the answer, every finding with the stage that fixes it, and what was checked. Read before writing any FSH, CQL or other L3 file for a guideline or an adaptation."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "l3-readiness",
      "dcterms:source": "smart-base/skills/content/authoring-who-smart-guidelines/l3-readiness.md",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
